---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AssignmentIdentity from "../../components/AssignmentIdentity.astro";
import MetricCard from "../../components/MetricCard.astro";
import ResultTable from "../../components/ResultTable.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/Figure.astro";
import { external } from "../../data/site";
import illustration from "../../../assignments/assignment-3/proposal/abo-samples.jpg";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
const proposal = readFileSync("assignments/assignment-3/proposal/dataset.md", "utf8");
const proposalRow = (label: string) => {
  const row = proposal.split("\n").find((line) => line.startsWith(`| ${label} |`));
  if (!row) throw new Error(`Missing proposal field: ${label}`);
  return row.split("|").slice(1, -1).map((cell) => cell.trim());
};
const proposalValue = (label: string) => proposalRow(label)[1];
const [pairCount, familyCount] = proposalValue("Selected pairs / product-family groups").split(" / ");
const subsetRows = ["Chair", "Grocery", "Rug", "Shoes", "Sofa"].map((label) => {
  const row = proposalRow(label);
  return { Class: row[0], Pairs: row[1], Train: row[2], Validation: row[3], Test: row[4] };
});
const total = subsetRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(row.Pairs.replaceAll(",", "")), 0).toLocaleString("en-US");
---
<BaseLayout title="Assignment 3" description="Amazon Berkeley Objects image–text product classification for CO3133 Assignment 3." current="a3">
  <section class="shell page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Assignment 3 · Image–text classification</p>
    <div class="page-status"><span class="status status-planned">M1 proposal available</span><small>Pending instructor approval</small></div>
    <h1>Multimodal Deep Learning</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Product classification using paired ABO catalog images and English titles: unimodal baselines, simple fusion, and learned gated fusion under a shared evaluation protocol.</p>
  </section>
  <AssignmentIdentity />
  <section class="shell"><div class="metric-grid">
    <MetricCard label="Dataset scope" value={total} detail="Paired products in five selected classes" accent={true} />
    <MetricCard label="Fixed split" value={proposalValue("Train / validation / test")} detail="Train / validation / test · product-family groups · seed 42" />
    <MetricCard label="Milestone" value="M1" detail="Dataset Proposal · instructor approval pending" />
  </div></section>
  <section class="shell article-layout">
    <article>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Problem statement</h2>
        <p>Given a product's main catalog image and original English title, predict Chair, Grocery, Rug, Shoes, or Sofa. Each prediction concerns one canonical product. The study will compare image-only and text-only baselines with concatenation and gated fusion, evaluating predictive quality alongside compute cost.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Dataset description and EDA</h2>
        <p>Amazon Berkeley Objects (ABO) provides 147,702 product listings and 398,212 catalog images. Images and metadata are released under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Both modalities are joined through the same product record and main-image identifier.</p>
        <ResultTable caption="ABO five-class subset and grouped split" rows={subsetRows} columns={[{key:"Class",label:"Class"},{key:"Pairs",label:"Pairs"},{key:"Train",label:"Train"},{key:"Validation",label:"Validation"},{key:"Test",label:"Test"}]} />
        <p>The metadata audit identifies {proposalValue("Canonical candidate pairs in five classes")} canonical candidates. It excludes {proposalValue("Mixed-category family groups excluded")} and caps Grocery at 3,000 while preserving complete groups. The selection contains {pairCount} pairs in {familyCount} family groups; no group spans partitions.</p>
        <div class="result-grid">
          <Figure src={illustration} alt="Two real catalog images for each selected ABO class: Chair, Grocery, Rug, Shoes, and Sofa" caption="Ten training examples, two per class. Images © Amazon.com, ABO, CC BY 4.0; resized and arranged with class labels for illustration." />
        </div>
        <p>The ten illustration pairs were retrieved, decoded, and inspected alongside their titles. Two images contain multiple room/seating objects, illustrating target ambiguity. Original metadata spans widths 166–3,000 and heights 70–2,560 pixels; sampled downscaled images span 118–256 by 95–256 pixels. Title lengths range from 1 to 24 words, with median 11.</p>
        <p>Grocery is the largest selected class; Sofa has 281 pairs and 28 test examples. Titles may directly name the product type. Full image validation, perceptual-duplicate review, and token-length/truncation analysis remain part of preparation.</p>
        <p>Source: <a href="https://amazon-berkeley-objects.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/index.html">official ABO dataset</a>, introduced by <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.06199">Collins et al. (CVPR 2022)</a>. Credit for source data belongs to Amazon.com and the dataset creators. Version, license, scope, and approval are documented in the <a href={external.a3Proposal}>Dataset Proposal</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Methodology</h2>
        <p>Images are converted to RGB, resized with preserved aspect ratio, padded on white to 224×224, and ImageNet-normalized. English titles use the DistilBERT uncased tokenizer with at most 64 tokens and attention masks. Only the original image/title enter the model; category fields, identifiers, and illustration labels do not.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Planned configurations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Configuration</th><th scope="col">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Image only</td><td>Frozen ImageNet ResNet-18, 512-dimensional features, five-class head</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Text only</td><td>Frozen DistilBERT, masked mean-pooled 768-dimensional features, five-class head</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Simple fusion</td><td>Concatenated features, 256-unit ReLU MLP and classifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Improved fusion</td><td>256-dimensional modality projections, learned sigmoid gate and classifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gate ablation</td><td>Same projections/classifier with equal fixed modality weights</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>Keep pretrained encoders in evaluation mode, including BatchNorm buffers/dropout; train only heads, projections, and gates. Train unimodal heads separately, then fusion heads using the same frozen encoder features. All configurations use cross-entropy with identical training-derived class weights. Missing raw modalities exclude a pair from the benchmark; diagnostic modality removal is separate.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Experimental setup</h2>
        <p>Connect products sharing an image, normalized identical title, or specific brand/model key. Canonicalize marketplace copies by product ID, excluding inconsistent labels, and keep each retained family in one split. Ten-fold stratified group allocation with seed 42 assigns fold 0 to test, fold 1 to validation, and the remaining folds to training: <strong>{proposalValue("Train / validation / test")}</strong>.</p>
        <p>Initial settings: AdamW, learning rate 0.001, weight decay 0.0001, batch size 32, maximum 20 epochs per configuration. Reset random seeds for each run. Select the highest validation macro-F1 checkpoint, then lower validation loss and earlier epoch. Keep manifests, preprocessing, weights, loss weighting, optimizer, budget, and selection rules fixed across fusion comparisons.</p>
        <p>Budget approximately 8 GB GPU memory, 10 GB storage, and 1–3 GPU-hours including feature extraction; confirm with a pilot. Record actual hardware/software, pretrained revisions, configs, seeds, epoch logs, run IDs, checkpoint hashes, and commit/tag. Main experiments begin after instructor approval.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <p>No experimental results are available at M1. Planned outputs include accuracy, macro-F1, per-class metrics, confusion matrices, learning curves, prediction examples, parameters, feature-extraction/head-training time, inference latency, and peak memory. Dataset statistics above are preliminary data-audit findings.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Comparison and discussion</h2>
        <p>Compare unimodal baselines, concatenation, and gated fusion. The controlled ablation changes learned gating to equal fixed weights while retaining the projection/classifier design and training protocol. State hypotheses, changed/fixed factors, metrics, and decision criteria. Account for capacity differences and compute cost; multimodal performance need not exceed the stronger unimodal baseline.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Error analysis</h2>
        <p>Inspect agreement, rescue, and conflict cases across modalities. Analyze multi-object room scenes, similar furniture, title/category words, packaging text, minority-class errors, and brand/background shortcuts. Report counts and examples. Missing-modality inference interventions are labelled separately from trained unimodal baselines; gate values alone are not causal evidence.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Limitations and conclusion</h2>
        <p>The scope covers five product types, English titles, one seed, and frozen encoders. Classes are imbalanced, titles can be highly predictive, and room scenes can include several product types. Preliminary sample review does not establish full-dataset integrity. The smaller Sofa test support limits per-class precision of estimates.</p>
        <p>The Dataset Proposal is available for instructor review. Training, report, slides, video, and checkpoints or reconstruction instructions are planned deliverables.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
    <aside class="side-stack"><section class="resource-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Resources</p><h2>Deliverables</h2>
      <a class="resource-link" href={external.a3Readme}><span>M1 source README</span><b>Open ↗</b></a>
      <a class="resource-link" href={external.a3Proposal}><span>Dataset proposal <span class="status status-planned">Pending approval</span></span><b>Open ↗</b></a>
      <div class="pending">Training source code · pending</div>
      <div class="pending">Checkpoints / reconstruction · pending implementation</div>
      <div class="pending">Final report · pending</div>
      <div class="pending">Slides · pending</div>
      <div class="pending">YouTube video · pending</div>
    </section></aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
